    "annotations_dropped": [
      {
        "annotation_id": "246ca8f1d066421e9c671fe705f9a50f_35",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As per the provisions of Section 195 of the Cr.P.C., no Court can take cognizance of the offence punishable under Section 188 of the IPC and here in this case no such compliance is made when the Food Safety Officer who promulgated the order"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f24caaf58f8b4608b9338f27cbee9498_38",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, it would be unjust to ask the applicant to face the trial and therefore, he seeks quashment of the FIR and the charge-sheet."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c4c07d77842e44e08597c2ba7ea8978e_42",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "After evaluating various decisions, it has been held that Section 89 of the FSSA indicates the intention to give overriding effect over all the food related laws."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "551cd3db74c14424b092979c1a6efbcf_43",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The main section clearly gives overriding effect when the offences under Sections 272 and 273 of IPC are made out."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "84fcefcea2724da9abd7aac295ed954f_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Even the offence under Section 59 of the FSSA will be attracted which is more stringent and therefore, by virtue of Section 89 of the FSSA, the Section 59 of the said Act which is overriding the provisions of Sections 272 and 273 of IPC, th"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2d9f6967f95c4df3903bc0a151620e53_45",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "6. Herein in this case, the police have invoked Section 59(1) of the FSSA as well as Section 273 of IPC."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "76ebda7582d64ab3aa03b61d8bd7bc09_46",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In view of clear pronouncement by Hon'ble Apex Court in Ram Nath (supra) both the sections cannot stand together."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "77d9755c85854d0aa471e51d1bc68166_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The prosecution for Section 273 of IPC cannot be allowed to be proceeded further in the present case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "de538789bcb641118116dc312e1e1915_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "7. As regards Section 59(1) of the FSSA is concerned, it contemplates filing of complaint by the Competent Authority under the said Act and not by police."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b4e0ae1c41f94d97b06824b39c008266_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Sections 41 and 42 of the FSSA makes it mandatory to follow the procedure required for the prosecution that too by the officers mentioned in the Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "96c17a1065af4d8f97cc2e9aec794f5a_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n6 apl198.24+J.odt"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8f4d2f815d0346b4b5ebf43795840286_51",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, the prosecution for the said offence under Section 59 of FSSA also cannot be allowed to proceed in the present case, as it is by a police officer."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e0969e9fe894403ba6c2484983bec08d_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nVaibhav S/O Bhaskar Bhoyar And 2 Others vs The State Of Mah. Thr. Pso, Nagbhid Ps, ... on 26 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/15782553/\n3 8."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "375d8c7d1d344076bf1196e812fdd0a7_53",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Now, as regards Section 188 of IPC is concerned; Section 195 Cr.P.C. puts some embargo on the powers of the Court to take cognizance of the offence punishable under Section 188 of IPC, except upon the complaint by the Competent Authority."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4bc045ede7dd4d9da02df357c265b19f_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Here the said Assistant Sub Inspector attached to Nagbhid Police Station cannot be said to be the Competent Authority."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "85a36d85ed21484ca73a24b236c763b1_55",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However, distinction can be made as regards the filing of complaint and taking of cognizance."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c89c0534363e4432b8ee7668ca873de7_56",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Filing of complaint is not prohibited, but taking cognizance of the said complaint which is filed by any other person than the Competent Authority is prohibited."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8fd756430056412a80ac73ab492ff11a_57",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "We are not aware as to whether the learned Magistrate has taken cognizance of the said offence or not."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "997d66c999674692b597d452a4d77401_58",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "For that purpose we would like to consider the facts of the case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "eb736846011d487fb0f5026fd66d6255_59",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "From the contents of the FIR and the statements of witnesses, we could gather that the present applicants were the passengers in the said vehicle."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "689d5300037e479b85a3e6660586a329_60",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The spot panchnama would clearly disclose that seven gunny bags were found in the dickey of the Wagon R. The investigation papers further do not show that there was investigation in respect of 7 apl198.24+J.odt owner of the vehicle and it a"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5ac830bd4de24625814e8d28ba4af3a6_61",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is not the case of the prosecution that any one of the applicants was driving the said vehicle."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f30135011bdb4dd6826947c80d250700_62",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "If they were merely passengers then it cannot be said that they were having knowledge of the articles kept in dickey."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "871078abc8e542a38719f09bf1cd1a4f_63",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The concept of conscious possession is missing and therefore, it cannot be said that the facts enumerated are attracted to the offence under Section 188 of IPC."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5862027b60f54074b9ccb3f82c75ecb6_64",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus, taking into consideration all the above reasons stated, now it would be unjust to ask the applicants to face the trial with such evidence."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "cafcba7067364541b6a521b4630b5b68_65",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Hence, case is made out to allow the applications."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "eac6066bd2664770968efd10045913c2_66",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. Accordingly, both the applications stand allowed."
